{
  "_readme": [
    "Cross-implementation parity fixture for reward arithmetic.",
    "",
    "Two implementations answer 'what does this card pay on this spend':",
    "  - packages/pandapay_domain  (Dart) ranks cards BEFORE a purchase.",
    "  - api/src/reward_math.js    (JS)   records what was earned AFTER one.",
    "",
    "They drifted, and both drifts showed up as wrong money on screen: the",
    "server attached caps to categories with NULL acting as a wildcard (so a",
    "rent payment consumed a grocery cap), and recorded value at the nominal",
    "rate with no cap blending at all (so 'earned this month' over-reported",
    "forever once a cap was spent).",
    "",
    "This file is the shared contract. Both test suites read it and assert",
    "the SAME expected numbers:",
    "  - packages/pandapay_domain/test/reward_parity_test.dart",
    "  - api/test/reward_math.test.js",
    "",
    "A change to reward arithmetic that only lands on one side fails here.",
    "Amounts are rupees. Rates are in the unit each rule names.",
    "",
    "Card fields use the snake_case wire shape (v_card_catalogue_export), so",
    "the Dart side decodes them through the same unmodified CardProductJson",
    "parsers a live GET /catalogue response goes through."
  ],
  "scenarios": [
